# Keeps this repo lean when it is used as a Docker BUILD CONTEXT by
# tds-gateway-api's Dockerfile (see its `additional_contexts`).
#
# Only the PHP half is consumed there: composer.json plus php/. The JS half and
# the installed dependencies are pure transfer cost — without this file a single
# extension shipped 150 MB+ of node_modules/vendor/.git into the build, and the
# context transfer alone took longer than the rest of the image put together.
#
# Two entries are here for a sharper reason than size — both bake LOCAL STATE
# into the image and make the container lie about itself:
#
#   .env  is a local dev secret. The container entrypoint sees it, logs
#         "keeping existing .env" and skips writing the container defaults, so
#         the service comes up pointed at a database that does not exist there.
#   var/  is runtime state. It holds the in-process auto-migrator's
#         `.migrated-<hash>` marker — copied in, the migrator believes a brand
#         new, empty database is already migrated and silently skips every
#         migration. The symptom is a service that boots green and then 500s on
#         the first query with "Base table or view not found".
.git
node_modules
vendor
dist
var
.claude
.astro
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
